Data: Smart Hospital Queue Solution App

The Data folder contains all the primary data collected and used during the
research phase of the project. This data forms the foundation for
understanding user behavior, identifying pain points, and making informed
design decisions.

As part of the Empathize stage, a survey was designed and conducted using
Google Forms to gather real user experiences related to hospital waiting times
and environments. The survey focused on key aspects such as patient anxiety
levels, waiting duration, comfort, and expectations for improvement.

The collected responses were then organized and analyzed using Google
Sheets. This helped in identifying patterns and trends, such as common issues
faced by patients (e.g., long waiting times, lack of engagement, and uncertainty
about queue status). These insights directly contributed to the creation of
empathy maps, personas, and the final problem statement.

Providing both the survey form and the response dataset ensures transparency
and demonstrates that the solution is based on real user data.

